      "writtenOn": "2023-04-18T12:33:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess you\u0027re thinking of the Arm Architecture Calls? There is already an enum `psci::smccc::arch::error::Error` for those, but this error type is for the KVM HVC calls not the Arm Architecture Calls. (Also the Arm Architecture Calls return values are all defined to be 32-bit, while the KVM calls are defined to have 64-bit return values.)\n\nFrom the KVM documentation I\u0027ve found, there seem to be only two possible error values, which I\u0027ve implemented here. According to http://cs/h/android/kernel/common/+/android14-5.15:Documentation/virt/kvm/arm/hypercalls.rst the memory sharing calls can return -3 for invalid parameter, and according to https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/common/+/android14-5.15:Documentation/virt/kvm/arm/mmio-guard.rst the MMIO guard calls can return -1 for not supported. There are no other error codes documented.",
      "parentUuid": "5cc47311_8ebc3d29",
